{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 2, :comments ["<b>And we shall live and not die.</b> The reason for the doubling: it intends to say that if they do not do so, they will be liable for their lives in the judgment of the Most High, and so they are dead in this world and sentenced to the world to come; and by exerting themselves in the matter, they shall live in this world and not die in the world to come." "<b>Or</b> it may intend in this manner: <b>and we shall live</b> — or at least <b>and not die</b>; and the intention is that if they succeed in purchasing grain in abundance and overflow, they will live in the normal manner of life, and if they do not obtain enough, they will at least obtain enough to save their lives from death by famine."], :book :genesis, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 42, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:47:51.275250537Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}